From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:52:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a real Configure entry point for Pile-On
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pile-On has no "hinges panel" so it never got a Configure button on its
own page — its only settings UI was EnablePileOnModal, and that was
enable-only with no way to reopen it afterward. Reused it instead of
building a second form:

- enable-worker-modal.tsx: EnablePileOnModal takes a new configureMode
  flag plus initialSmsPlatform/initialAdDataPlatform. In configure mode
  the title, copy, submit label ("Save changes"), and the Ask Teammates
  seed message all reflect editing existing settings, and "Skip for
  now" (meaningless once already configured) becomes "Cancel".
- enable-pile-on.ts: the stack write only fired for a non-"none" value,
  which was right for the initial Enable flow's untouched dropdowns but
  silently dropped a deliberate "turn this back off" selection in
  Configure. Now writes whenever a field is explicitly passed,
  including "none".
- pile-on-configure-button.tsx (new): the same small icon-only trigger
  every other skill's Configure button uses, wired to the modal in
  configureMode with the engagement's current stack values.
- skills/pile-on/page.tsx: selects stack, renders the new button next
  to the title like every other skill page already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
